<article class="env-lemma" id="02HQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02HQ">Lemma <span data-tag="02HQ">10.131.11</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. Let $I \subset S$ be an ideal. Let $n \geq 1$ be an integer. Set $S' = S/I^{n + 1}$. The map $\Omega _{S/R} \to \Omega _{S'/R}$ induces an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Omega _{S/R} \otimes _ S S/I^ n \longrightarrow \Omega _{S'/R} \otimes _{S'} S/I^ n.  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00RU" data-tag="00RU">10.131.9</a> and the fact that $\text{d}(I^{n + 1}) \subset I^ n\Omega _{S/R}$ by the Leibniz rule for $\text{d}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>